The first end-to-end script run caught a smoke-program assembly bug: `solution.mpy` closes `Module(...)` on the same line as the final function, so deleting the last line also deleted part of `do_algebra`. I’m switching the assembly step to remove only the final closing parenthesis, preserving the exact translated function.
apply patch
